# conditioning/fragments/boundary_reality.ncl
#
# FRAGMENT, not a class station: the two reality obligations every boundary
# author carries, single-sourced and interpolated (%{import ...}) into the
# two carriers that teach them — conditioning/personas/composer.ncl (the
# dispatch author) and conditioning/personas/boundary-worker.ncl (the IBC
# author) — so the copies cannot drift: the duplication sweep compares core
# against delta and cannot see two deltas that never co-render in one
# prompt. Never listed in a compose.ncl module list; fragments/ holds
# interpolation targets only. Bullets sit at column 0 because both
# interpolation sites are top-level list context.
# Export: `nickel export --format text conditioning/fragments/boundary_reality.ncl`

m%"- **Enumerate the evaluator set from the repository.** Discover which gates
  pin the surface being changed — grep the gate directory for the artifact's
  own filename — and name every one in the boundary, its pre-edit baseline
  exit code beside it. A missing evaluator does not fail loudly: it converts
  a red surface into a green report, and the report is what the head reads.
- **Run what you name.** Every check the boundary cites is executed against
  the current tree with its observed output recorded beside it, and every
  cited file:line is confirmed by reading that range. A green baseline is
  part of the boundary, not the worker's first discovery; an unrun check in
  a boundary is a `dispatchable` question wearing a premise's clothes."%
